<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    DEVELOPER VERIFICATION TOOL — NOT PART OF THE PRODUCT. See tools/probes/README.md.

    Data Import — etap I4 (docs/design/data-import.md §6). Proves the WRITE path against a live FB5 engine.

    ⭐ It differs from DataImportWriteProbe (etap I0) in the one way that matters: I0 measured the ENGINE and
    the DRIVER with raw ADO.NET, because no production import code existed yet. This probe runs the REAL
    production stack — ImportPipeline -> FirebirdImportWriter -> FirebirdImportErrorMapper — so what it proves
    is not "Firebird behaves like this" but "OUR CODE behaves like Firebird told us it would". Two questions
    the user asked for explicitly:

      (E) does every failure class map to the right ImportErrorKind, from the GDS VECTOR rather than
          ErrorCode — and does the report name the right SOURCE row?
      (B) does FbBatchCommand behave as I0 measured, in particular the 1:1 error indexing and the
          MultiError <-> ImportErrorPolicy mapping?

    Runs against Lab/EmberTern_Lab.fdb (the IMP_* zoo added in I4). It only touches IMP_* tables and cleans
    them out before each case, so the debugger/metadata zoo is never disturbed.

    Deliberately NOT in EmberTern.slnx: it needs a live server and a password, which the hermetic test suite
    must never need.

    How to run: see the header of Program.cs (an XML comment cannot carry the double dash the CLI needs).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <!-- The probe is a scratch tool; a warning here must not block a verification run. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\src\EmberTern.Core\EmberTern.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\src\EmberTern.Firebird\EmberTern.Firebird.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
